\section{Language of returned text}{

\code{qesR.lang} sets the language of messages only: it never sets the \code{lang}
argument of a function, which is given in each call and does not mean the
same thing everywhere:
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=qes_harmonize]{qes_harmonize()}}: \code{"en"} (default) or \code{"fr"}, the language of factor
levels, variable labels and target populations; codes do not change;
\item \code{\link[=qes_spec]{qes_spec()}}: \code{"en"} (default) or \code{"fr"}, the language of labels,
definitions, grade reasons and notes;
\item \code{\link[=qes_codebook]{qes_codebook()}} and \code{\link[=qes_question]{qes_question()}}: \code{NULL} (default), the study's
own language, or \code{"en"}, \code{"fr"}; the language of question text (labels
are always the file's);
\item \code{\link[=qes_search]{qes_search()}}: \code{"both"} (default), \code{"en"} or \code{"fr"}, the languages
searched and the language of the \code{question} column;
\item \code{\link[=qes_cite]{qes_cite()}}: \code{"en"} (default) or \code{"fr"}, the language of the few words
qesR adds to citations;
\item \code{\link[=qes_docs]{qes_docs()}} and \code{\link[=qes_download]{qes_download()}}: a filter, the document languages to
keep (\code{NULL}, the default, keeps all).
}
}

\section{Conditions}{

Errors, warnings and messages have classes, so code can react to them with
\code{tryCatch()} or \code{withCallingHandlers()} without matching message text.
Errors inherit from \code{qesR_error}:
\describe{
\item{\code{qesR_error_input}}{an invalid argument (fields \code{arg}, \code{value}),
including files that \code{\link[=qes_download]{qes_download()}} would overwrite (field
\code{paths});}
\item{\code{qesR_error_unknown_study}}{an unknown study code (fields \code{study},
\code{suggestions});}
\item{\code{qesR_error_unknown_variable}}{an unknown column (fields
\code{variables}, \code{suggestions});}
\item{\code{qesR_error_ambiguous_file}}{a \code{file} pattern that matches no data
file of the study, or several (fields \code{study}, \code{pattern},
\code{candidates});}
\item{\code{qesR_error_network}}{a failed download (fields \code{url}, \code{attempts},
and \code{parent}, the root cause). Its subclasses are
\code{qesR_error_http} (an HTTP error status; fields \code{status},
\code{retry_after}, \code{server_message}), itself the parent of
\code{qesR_error_http_refused} (the server refused the automated request;
field \code{manual_path}); \code{qesR_error_tls} (the secure connection failed;
qesR never retries without TLS certificate checks); and
\code{qesR_error_offline} (the server's name could not be resolved);}
\item{\code{qesR_error_source}}{a problem with the files served for a study
(fields \code{study}, \code{file_id}), such as a file missing from the latest
version of its deposit; subclasses \code{qesR_error_checksum} (a file
that does not match its catalog md5; fields \code{expected}, \code{actual}) and
\code{qesR_error_rowcount} (a data file whose rows and columns differ from
the catalog; fields \code{expected}, \code{actual});}
\item{\code{qesR_error_cache}}{a cache directory that is missing or is not a
qesR cache (fields \code{path}, \code{reason});}
\item{\code{qesR_error_no_provenance}}{an object that no longer records which
study it comes from, passed to \code{\link[=qes_cite]{qes_cite()}} or \code{\link[=qes_provenance]{qes_provenance()}}, or
a provenance level the object does not record (field \code{level});}
\item{\code{qesR_error_dependency}}{a suggested package that a function
needs is not installed, such as \pkg{survey} for \code{\link[=qes_design]{qes_design()}}
(field \code{package});}
\item{\code{qesR_error_spec}}{a harmonization spec with errors, or data that
